A directory argument lists the supported files under it, nested ones included, and skips the unsupported `raw.txt`; a Markdown file without frontmatter prints its first heading.
== args
input/src
== file input/src/has-comment.md
---
description: Has summary.
---
# one
== file input/src/nested/no-summary.md
# two
== file input/src/raw.txt
plain text
== stdout
glob view: input/src
input/src/has-comment.md (4 lines): description: "Has summary."
input/src/nested/no-summary.md (1 line): # two
== stderr
== exit 0
